}", "recovery_added_pnums": []}, "methods": {"selected_paragraphs_json": "[{"pnum": 18, "paragraph_text": "Methods", "sentences": [{"sid": "S39", "text": "Methods"}]}, {"pnum": 19, "paragraph_text": "Trial design and participants", "sentences": [{"sid": "S40", "text": "Trial design and participants"}]}, {"pnum": 20, "paragraph_text": "In this randomised controlled trial, patients were recruited from 37 of 45 renal units in acute hospitals throughout the UK that obtained local ethical approval. Inclusion criteria were: age 18–75 years; biopsy-proven diagnosis of membranous nephropathy (we did not impose a limit on the time since biopsy), regarded as idiopathic with no evidence of an underlying cause (such as drugs, infections, or tumours); and serum or plasma creatinine concentration of less than 300 μmol/L together with a 20% or greater decline in excretory renal function (measured by creatinine clearance or estimated with the Cockcroft-Gault calculation, and later by the Modification of Diet in Renal Disease [MDRD] formula13) that was based on at least three measurements over a period of 3 months or longer within the 2 years before study entry.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S41", "text": "In this randomised controlled trial, patients were recruited from 37 of 45 renal units in acute hospitals throughout the UK that obtained local ethical approval."}, {"sid": "S42", "text": "Inclusion criteria were: age 18–75 years; biopsy-proven diagnosis of membranous nephropathy (we did not impose a limit on the time since biopsy), regarded as idiopathic with no evidence of an underlying cause (such as drugs, infections, or tumours); and serum or plasma creatinine concentration of less than 300 μmol/L together with a 20% or greater decline in excretory renal function (measured by creatinine clearance or estimated with the Cockcroft-Gault calculation, and later by the Modification of Diet in Renal Disease [MDRD] formula13) that was based on at least three measurements over a period of 3 months or longer within the 2 years before study entry."}]}, {"pnum": 21, "paragraph_text": "We excluded patients whose membranous nephropathy was a result of secondary causes (defined according to usual clinical practice). Other exclusion criteria were: known infection with hepatitis B or C virus or HIV; known malignant disease; positive antibodies to double-stranded DNA; current treatment with gold, penicillamine, non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs, cytotoxic drugs, or ciclosporin; more than 3 months' treatment with corticosteroids in the preceding 2 years; pregnancy or unreliable contraception; or a previous adverse reaction to prednisolone, methylprednisolone, chlorambucil or ciclosporin.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S43", "text": "We excluded patients whose membranous nephropathy was a result of secondary causes (defined according to usual clinical practice)."}, {"sid": "S44", "text": "Other exclusion criteria were: known infection with hepatitis B or C virus or HIV; known malignant disease; positive antibodies to double-stranded DNA; current treatment with gold, penicillamine, non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs, cytotoxic drugs, or ciclosporin; more than 3 months' treatment with corticosteroids in the preceding 2 years; pregnancy or unreliable contraception; or a previous adverse reaction to prednisolone, methylprednisolone, chlorambucil or ciclosporin."}]}, {"pnum": 23, "paragraph_text": "Randomisation", "sentences": [{"sid": "S48", "text": "Randomisation"}]}, {"pnum": 24, "paragraph_text": "Eligible patients were randomly assigned by a member of staff in the clinical trials office at the Glasgow Royal Infirmary, Glasgow, UK, who was not otherwise involved in the trial. A random numbers table had been prepared to allocate patients to one of three groups: supportive therapy alone, supportive therapy plus 6 months of prednisolone and chlorambucil, or supportive therapy plus 12 months of ciclosporin. Treatment allocation was communicated by fax to the clinician entering the patient into the trial. We did not attempt to mask patients or investigators.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S49", "text": "Eligible patients were randomly assigned by a member of staff in the clinical trials office at the Glasgow Royal Infirmary, Glasgow, UK, who was not otherwise involved in the trial."}, {"sid": "S50", "text": "A random numbers table had been prepared to allocate patients to one of three groups: supportive therapy alone, supportive therapy plus 6 months of prednisolone and chlorambucil, or supportive therapy plus 12 months of ciclosporin."}, {"sid": "S51", "text": "Treatment allocation was communicated by fax to the clinician entering the patient into the trial."}, {"sid": "S52", "text": "We did not attempt to mask patients or investigators."}]}, {"pnum": 25, "paragraph_text": "Procedures", "sentences": [{"sid": "S53", "text": "Procedures"}]}, {"pnum": 26, "paragraph_text": "We recorded baseline data for the supportive treatment alone group at randomisation, because these patients were effectively continuing their existing management. In the two groups receiving immunosuppressive treatment in addition to supportive therapy, baseline data were recorded when the new treatment began. We could not always start immunosuppressive treatment immediately after randomisation because the new treatments had to be prescribed and delivered.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S54", "text": "We recorded baseline data for the supportive treatment alone group at randomisation, because these patients were effectively continuing their existing management."}, {"sid": "S55", "text": "In the two groups receiving immunosuppressive treatment in addition to supportive therapy, baseline data were recorded when the new treatment began."}, {"sid": "S56", "text": "We could not always start immunosuppressive treatment immediately after randomisation because the new treatments had to be prescribed and delivered."}]}, {"pnum": 27, "paragraph_text": "The treatment schedules were based on best available evidence at the time. All patients received supportive therapy, including renin-angiotensin blockade, statins, and anticoagulants as indicated. Those assigned to supportive therapy plus 6 months' prednisolone and chorambucil11 received intravenous methyl prednisolone 1 g per day for 3 consecutive days then oral prednisolone 0·5 mg/kg per day for 28 days during months 1, 3, and 5. Intravenous prednisolone was administered in hospital. During months 2, 4, and 6, patients received oral chlorambucil at a starting dose of 0·15 mg/kg per day. We gave this reduced dose because the parent drug and its metabolites are renally excreted and our preliminary work14 had shown that a dose of 0·2 mg/kg per day was poorly tolerated in patients with impaired excretory renal function. We reduced the dose further if the patient developed leucopenia (weekly full blood counts were advised) and interrupted it if leucopenia was severe.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S57", "text": "The treatment schedules were based on best available evidence at the time."}, {"sid": "S58", "text": "All patients received supportive therapy, including renin-angiotensin blockade, statins, and anticoagulants as indicated."}, {"sid": "S59", "text": "Those assigned to supportive therapy plus 6 months' prednisolone and chorambucil11 received intravenous methyl prednisolone 1 g per day for 3 consecutive days then oral prednisolone 0·5 mg/kg per day for 28 days during months 1, 3, and 5."}, {"sid": "S60", "text": "Intravenous prednisolone was administered in hospital."}, {"sid": "S61", "text": "During months 2, 4, and 6, patients received oral chlorambucil at a starting dose of 0·15 mg/kg per day."}, {"sid": "S62", "text": "We gave this reduced dose because the parent drug and its metabolites are renally excreted and our preliminary work14 had shown that a dose of 0·2 mg/kg per day was poorly tolerated in patients with impaired excretory renal function."}, {"sid": "S63", "text": "We reduced the dose further if the patient developed leucopenia (weekly full blood counts were advised) and interrupted it if leucopenia was severe."}]}, {"pnum": 28, "paragraph_text": "Those assigned to supportive therapy plus 12 months' of ciclosporin received a starting dose of 5 mg/kg per day,12 adjusted according to trough blood concentrations of the drug to achieve a concentration of 100–200 μg/L. We reduced the dose if toxicity was evident.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S64", "text": "Those assigned to supportive therapy plus 12 months' of ciclosporin received a starting dose of 5 mg/kg per day,12 adjusted according to trough blood concentrations of the drug to achieve a concentration of 100–200 μg/L."}, {"sid": "S65", "text": "We reduced the dose if toxicity was evident."}]}, {"pnum": 29, "paragraph_text": "We followed up patients until they met the primary endpoint, or for a minimum of 3 years if they did not do so. The trial was not formally analysed until 3 years after all patients had begun treatment. All surviving trial patients remain under routine follow-up at their renal units.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S66", "text": "We followed up patients until they met the primary endpoint, or for a minimum of 3 years if they did not do so."}, {"sid": "S67", "text": "The trial was not formally analysed until 3 years after all patients had begun treatment."}, {"sid": "S68", "text": "All surviving trial patients remain under routine follow-up at their renal units."}]}, {"pnum": 30, "paragraph_text": "The primary endpoint was a further 20% decline in excretory renal function from baseline readings, calculated in all patients with the Cockcroft-Gault equation (standard methodology at the start of the trial).", "sentences": [{"sid": "S69", "text": "The primary endpoint was a further 20% decline in excretory renal function from baseline readings, calculated in all patients with the Cockcroft-Gault equation (standard methodology at the start of the trial)."}]}, {"pnum": 31, "paragraph_text": "Secondary endpoints were proteinuria (measured with 24-h urinary collections or estimated from protein–creatinine ratios by multiplying the ratio [in mg/mmol] by 10) and severe adverse events. The primary investigator (PWM) identified which adverse events were serious and categorised them according to the most affected body system. We report all serious adverse events as defined by the Medicines and Healthcare products Regulatory Agency (MHRA) guidance15—(ie, any adverse event, adverse reaction, or unexpected adverse reaction that results in death, is life-threatening, results in admission to hospital or extends the length of an existing hospital stay, results in persistent or serious disability or incapacity, or consists of a congenital anomaly or birth defect). We also regarded as serious other important medical events that might have jeopardised the patient or needed intervention to prevent one of these outcomes. We recorded information about deaths and development of end-stage renal disease.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S70", "text": "Secondary endpoints were proteinuria (measured with 24-h urinary collections or estimated from protein–creatinine ratios by multiplying the ratio [in mg/mmol] by 10) and severe adverse events."}, {"sid": "S71", "text": "The primary investigator (PWM) identified which adverse events were serious and categorised them according to the most affected body system."}, {"sid": "S72", "text": "We report all serious adverse events as defined by the Medicines and Healthcare products Regulatory Agency (MHRA) guidance15—(ie, any adverse event, adverse reaction, or unexpected adverse reaction that results in death, is life-threatening, results in admission to hospital or extends the length of an existing hospital stay, results in persistent or serious disability or incapacity, or consists of a congenital anomaly or birth defect)."}, {"sid": "S73", "text": "We also regarded as serious other important medical events that might have jeopardised the patient or needed intervention to prevent one of these outcomes."}, {"sid": "S74", "text": "We recorded information about deaths and development of end-stage renal disease."}]}, {"pnum": 32, "paragraph_text": "In accordance with the Medical Research Council's guidelines for good clinical practice, a trial steering committee and a data monitoring committee were established to receive yearly reports for primary endpoints, adverse events, and deaths.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S75", "text": "In accordance with the Medical Research Council's guidelines for good clinical practice, a trial steering committee and a data monitoring committee were established to receive yearly reports for primary endpoints, adverse events, and deaths."}]}, {"pnum": 33, "paragraph_text": "Statistical analysis", "sentences": [{"sid": "S76", "text": "Statistical analysis"}]}, {"pnum": 34, "paragraph_text": "To have 90% power to detect a reduction in frequency of the primary endpoint from 80% in the supportive treatment group to 40% in the immunosuppression groups with p<0·05, we calculated that 35 patients would be needed in each group (105 in total). After allowing for an estimated dropout rate of 10%, we concluded that we needed to recruit 116 patients.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S77", "text": "To have 90% power to detect a reduction in frequency of the primary endpoint from 80% in the supportive treatment group to 40% in the immunosuppression groups with p<0·05, we calculated that 35 patients would be needed in each group (105 in total)."}, {"sid": "S78", "text": "After allowing for an estimated dropout rate of 10%, we concluded that we needed to recruit 116 patients."}]}, {"pnum": 35, "paragraph_text": "Primary analysis followed the principles of intention to treat, and secondary analysis assessed all patients who received at least one dose of treatment. Unless otherwise stated, p values and estimates of treatment effects are based on two-way comparisons. We did not make adjustments for multiple comparisons. We analysed time to further 20% decline in renal function by the log-rank test and calculated hazard ratios [HRs] with Cox proportional hazards regression. We used the log-rank test for other survival endpoints, and repeated measures analysis of variance fowr continuous longitudinal data (eg, proteinuria). We analysed serious adverse event data with the log-rank test on the basis of time to first serious adverse event. We did statistical analyses using SAS software (version 9.2).", "sentences": [{"sid": "S79", "text": "Primary analysis followed the principles of intention to treat, and secondary analysis assessed all patients who received at least one dose of treatment."}, {"sid": "S80", "text": "Unless otherwise stated, p values and estimates of treatment effects are based on two-way comparisons."}, {"sid": "S81", "text": "We did not make adjustments for multiple comparisons."}, {"sid": "S82", "text": "We analysed time to further 20% decline in renal function by the log-rank test and calculated hazard ratios [HRs] with Cox proportional hazards regression."}, {"sid": "S83", "text": "We used the log-rank test for other survival endpoints, and repeated measures analysis of variance fowr continuous longitudinal data (eg, proteinuria)."}, {"sid": "S84", "text": "We analysed serious adverse event data with the log-rank test on the basis of time to first serious adverse event."}, {"sid": "S85", "text": "We did statistical analyses using SAS software (version 9.2)."}]}]", "extraction_output_json": "{
