}", "recovery_added_pnums": []}, "results": {"selected_paragraphs_json": "[{"pnum": 39, "paragraph_text": "Results", "sentences": [{"sid": "S92", "text": "Results"}]}, {"pnum": 40, "paragraph_text": "Figure 1 Trial profile", "sentences": [{"sid": "S93", "text": "Figure 1 Trial profile"}]}, {"pnum": 41, "paragraph_text": "We randomly assigned 108 patients between April 1, 1998, and March 31, 2008, at a steady rate of about one patient per month (figure 1). We discovered that two patients were ineligible after randomisation, so no follow-up data are available for them, and they weren't included in the primary analysis. Of the 106 patients included in the intention-to-treat analysis, 37 were assigned to receive supportive therapy alone, 33 to prednisolone and chlorambucil, and 36 to ciclosporin. 37 of the 45 centres that obtained ethics approval entered patients into the trial.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S94", "text": "We randomly assigned 108 patients between April 1, 1998, and March 31, 2008, at a steady rate of about one patient per month (figure 1)."}, {"sid": "S95", "text": "We discovered that two patients were ineligible after randomisation, so no follow-up data are available for them, and they weren't included in the primary analysis."}, {"sid": "S96", "text": "Of the 106 patients included in the intention-to-treat analysis, 37 were assigned to receive supportive therapy alone, 33 to prednisolone and chlorambucil, and 36 to ciclosporin."}, {"sid": "S97", "text": "37 of the 45 centres that obtained ethics approval entered patients into the trial."}]}, {"pnum": 42, "paragraph_text": "Table 1 Baseline values", "sentences": [{"sid": "S98", "text": "Table 1 Baseline values"}]}, {"pnum": 43, "paragraph_text": "The groups had similar baseline measurements (table 1). Times between randomisation and baseline readings are longer in both immunosuppressive groups than in the supportive therapy alone group because of delays relating to prescription, delivery, and administration of treatment.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S99", "text": "The groups had similar baseline measurements (table 1)."}, {"sid": "S100", "text": "Times between randomisation and baseline readings are longer in both immunosuppressive groups than in the supportive therapy alone group because of delays relating to prescription, delivery, and administration of treatment."}]}, {"pnum": 44, "paragraph_text": "We classed deviations from the defined protocol, including starting dose of intervention drugs, as either minor (eg, dose reductions because of toxicity) or major (eg, cessation of treatment, including temporary interruptions, or administration of the wrong treatment). We did not classify a delay between randomisation and start of treatment as a default protocol deviation. However, two patients had excessive delays (2 and 3 months, respectively), and we classified both as major deviations.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S101", "text": "We classed deviations from the defined protocol, including starting dose of intervention drugs, as either minor (eg, dose reductions because of toxicity) or major (eg, cessation of treatment, including temporary interruptions, or administration of the wrong treatment)."}, {"sid": "S102", "text": "We did not classify a delay between randomisation and start of treatment as a default protocol deviation."}, {"sid": "S103", "text": "However, two patients had excessive delays (2 and 3 months, respectively), and we classified both as major deviations."}]}, {"pnum": 45, "paragraph_text": "Angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitor was given to 27 (82%) of 33 in the prednisolone and chlorambucil group, 36 (100%) of 36 patients in the ciclosporin group, and 34 (92%) of 37 of those who received supportive treatment only. We did not obtain information about angiotensin-receptor antagonist use.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S104", "text": "Angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitor was given to 27 (82%) of 33 in the prednisolone and chlorambucil group, 36 (100%) of 36 patients in the ciclosporin group, and 34 (92%) of 37 of those who received supportive treatment only."}, {"sid": "S105", "text": "We did not obtain information about angiotensin-receptor antagonist use."}]}, {"pnum": 46, "paragraph_text": "Figure 2 Kaplan-Meier analysis of further 20% decline in renal function", "sentences": [{"sid": "S106", "text": "Figure 2 Kaplan-Meier analysis of further 20% decline in renal function"}]}, {"pnum": 47, "paragraph_text": "Deaths were censored. GFR=glomerular filtration rate.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S107", "text": "Deaths were censored."}, {"sid": "S108", "text": "GFR=glomerular filtration rate."}]}, {"pnum": 48, "paragraph_text": "The rate of occurrence of a further 20% decline in excretory renal function from baseline was fastest in the ciclosporin group and slowest in the prednisolone and chlorambucil group (figure 2). Risk of a further 20% decline in renal function was significantly lower in the prednisolone and chlorambucil group than in the supportive therapy group (19 [58%] of 33 patients vs 31 [84%] of 37 patients, HR 0·44 [95% CI 0·24–0·78]; p=0·0042), with no significant difference noted between the ciclosporin group (29 [81%] of 36 patients) and supportive care group (HR 1·17 [0·70–1·95]; p=0·54). The difference in the proportion of patients who reached the primary endpoint across all three groups was significant (p=0·003 for the three-way comparison; figure 2).", "sentences": [{"sid": "S109", "text": "The rate of occurrence of a further 20% decline in excretory renal function from baseline was fastest in the ciclosporin group and slowest in the prednisolone and chlorambucil group (figure 2)."}, {"sid": "S110", "text": "Risk of a further 20% decline in renal function was significantly lower in the prednisolone and chlorambucil group than in the supportive therapy group (19 [58%] of 33 patients vs 31 [84%] of 37 patients, HR 0·44 [95% CI 0·24–0·78]; p=0·0042), with no significant difference noted between the ciclosporin group (29 [81%] of 36 patients) and supportive care group (HR 1·17 [0·70–1·95]; p=0·54)."}, {"sid": "S111", "text": "The difference in the proportion of patients who reached the primary endpoint across all three groups was significant (p=0·003 for the three-way comparison; figure 2)."}]}, {"pnum": 49, "paragraph_text": "Survival analysis showed no significant differences between groups: two (6·1%) of 33 patients in the prednisolone plus chlorambucil group died during the trial follow-up compared with two (5·6%) of 36 patients in the ciclosporin group and one (2·7%) of 37 in the supportive therapy group. We did not classify any deaths as likely to be related to trial treatments. Of the five deaths, two were due to myocardial infarction (one each in the prednisolone plus chlorambucil and ciclosporin groups), one to septicaemia (in the supportive treatment only group), and two to unknown causes.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S112", "text": "Survival analysis showed no significant differences between groups: two (6·1%) of 33 patients in the prednisolone plus chlorambucil group died during the trial follow-up compared with two (5·6%) of 36 patients in the ciclosporin group and one (2·7%) of 37 in the supportive therapy group."}, {"sid": "S113", "text": "We did not classify any deaths as likely to be related to trial treatments."}, {"sid": "S114", "text": "Of the five deaths, two were due to myocardial infarction (one each in the prednisolone plus chlorambucil and ciclosporin groups), one to septicaemia (in the supportive treatment only group), and two to unknown causes."}]}, {"pnum": 50, "paragraph_text": "Malignant disease was reported in two (6·1%) of 33 patients in the prednisolone plus chlorambucil group during follow-up: one had squamous-cell carcinoma of the skin and one had adenocarcinoma of the sigmoid colon. 11 patients reached end-stage renal disease: one (3·0%) of 33 in the prednisolone plus chlorambucil group compared with six (16·7%) of 36 in the ciclosporin group and four (10·8%) of 37 in the supportive therapy group.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S115", "text": "Malignant disease was reported in two (6·1%) of 33 patients in the prednisolone plus chlorambucil group during follow-up: one had squamous-cell carcinoma of the skin and one had adenocarcinoma of the sigmoid colon."}, {"sid": "S116", "text": "11 patients reached end-stage renal disease: one (3·0%) of 33 in the prednisolone plus chlorambucil group compared with six (16·7%) of 36 in the ciclosporin group and four (10·8%) of 37 in the supportive therapy group."}]}, {"pnum": 51, "paragraph_text": "Figure 3 Change in measured or calculated 24-h urinary protein", "sentences": [{"sid": "S117", "text": "Figure 3 Change in measured or calculated 24-h urinary protein"}]}, {"pnum": 52, "paragraph_text": "Datapoints show mean change in 24-h urinary protein from baseline; error bars show 95% CI. The numbers of patients from whom readings were taken at each timepoint are presented; variation in numbers was due to dropout and missing readings at those timepoints.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S118", "text": "Datapoints show mean change in 24-h urinary protein from baseline; error bars show 95% CI."}, {"sid": "S119", "text": "The numbers of patients from whom readings were taken at each timepoint are presented; variation in numbers was due to dropout and missing readings at those timepoints."}]}, {"pnum": 53, "paragraph_text": "The fall in proteinuria with time was greatest in the prednisolone plus chlorambucil group (figure 3). The difference in the mean reduction of protein in the urine for prednisolone and chlorambucil versus supportive therapy alone was −2·2 g in 24 h (p=0·014). The difference in the mean reduction for ciclosporin versus supportive care alone was −0·7 g in 24 h (p=0·46).", "sentences": [{"sid": "S120", "text": "The fall in proteinuria with time was greatest in the prednisolone plus chlorambucil group (figure 3)."}, {"sid": "S121", "text": "The difference in the mean reduction of protein in the urine for prednisolone and chlorambucil versus supportive therapy alone was −2·2 g in 24 h (p=0·014)."}, {"sid": "S122", "text": "The difference in the mean reduction for ciclosporin versus supportive care alone was −0·7 g in 24 h (p=0·46)."}]}, {"pnum": 54, "paragraph_text": "Table 2 Serious adverse events by treatment and body system affected", "sentences": [{"sid": "S123", "text": "Table 2 Serious adverse events by treatment and body system affected"}]}, {"pnum": 55, "paragraph_text": "We recorded 390 adverse events, of which 117 were deemed serious by PWM. These 117 events occurred in 54 patients (table 2). The number of patients with a serious adverse event by 1 year did not differ significantly between the ciclosporin and supportive care groups (17 [46%] of 37 patients in the ciclosporin group vs 11 [29%] of 38 in the supportive therapy only group; p=0·20), but the number of patients in the prednisolone and chlorambucil group with a serious adverse event by 1 year (17 [52%] of 33 patients) was significantly higher than in the supportive care group (p=0·048).", "sentences": [{"sid": "S124", "text": "We recorded 390 adverse events, of which 117 were deemed serious by PWM."}, {"sid": "S125", "text": "These 117 events occurred in 54 patients (table 2)."}, {"sid": "S126", "text": "The number of patients with a serious adverse event by 1 year did not differ significantly between the ciclosporin and supportive care groups (17 [46%] of 37 patients in the ciclosporin group vs 11 [29%] of 38 in the supportive therapy only group; p=0·20), but the number of patients in the prednisolone and chlorambucil group with a serious adverse event by 1 year (17 [52%] of 33 patients) was significantly higher than in the supportive care group (p=0·048)."}]}, {"pnum": 56, "paragraph_text": "Haematological events were leucopenia, anaemia, and thrombocytopenia, although we did not note any lymphomas or leukaemias. Dermatological effects included rash and shingles. Renal effects were mainly deterioration of excretory renal function or hyperkalaemia. Neurological effects were tremor and headache. Cardiovascular effects were hypertension, myocardial infarction, chest pain, and pulmonary embolus. Metabolic effects included impairment of glucose tolerance. Gastroenterological effects included nausea, vomiting, diarrhoea, bleeding, and pancreatitis. Infection included septicaemia, pneumonia, and cellulitis. Other effects included cataract, fractured humerus, hernia repairs, and pulmonary sarcoid. We acknowledge that some potential adverse effects of prednisolone plus chlorambucil and ciclosporin are more longlasting than the effects reported with supportive care alone, especially the risk of lymphoma or other malignant diseases.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S127", "text": "Haematological events were leucopenia, anaemia, and thrombocytopenia, although we did not note any lymphomas or leukaemias."}, {"sid": "S128", "text": "Dermatological effects included rash and shingles."}, {"sid": "S129", "text": "Renal effects were mainly deterioration of excretory renal function or hyperkalaemia."}, {"sid": "S130", "text": "Neurological effects were tremor and headache."}, {"sid": "S131", "text": "Cardiovascular effects were hypertension, myocardial infarction, chest pain, and pulmonary embolus."}, {"sid": "S132", "text": "Metabolic effects included impairment of glucose tolerance."}, {"sid": "S133", "text": "Gastroenterological effects included nausea, vomiting, diarrhoea, bleeding, and pancreatitis."}, {"sid": "S134", "text": "Infection included septicaemia, pneumonia, and cellulitis."}, {"sid": "S135", "text": "Other effects included cataract, fractured humerus, hernia repairs, and pulmonary sarcoid."}, {"sid": "S136", "text": "We acknowledge that some potential adverse effects of prednisolone plus chlorambucil and ciclosporin are more longlasting than the effects reported with supportive care alone, especially the risk of lymphoma or other malignant diseases."}]}]", "extraction_output_json": "{"article_id":"PMC3590447","section":"results","extractions":[{"item":"13a","pnum":40,"sid":"S93","score":0.9,"rationale":"The caption explicitly identifies Figure 1 as the trial profile documenting participant flow."},{"item":"13a","pnum":41,"sid":"S94","score":0.98,"rationale":"The sentence reports that 108 patients were randomly assigned."},{"item":"14a","pnum":41,"sid":"S94","score":0.99,"rationale":"The sentence gives the dates spanning randomisation and recruitment."},{"item":"13b","pnum":41,"sid":"S95","score":0.99,"rationale":"Two patients were found ineligible after randomisation and excluded because no follow-up data were available."},{"item":"13a","pnum":41,"sid":"S96","score":0.94,"rationale":"The sentence reports group-specific totals within the intention-to-treat population."},{"item":"16","pnum":41,"sid":"S96","score":0.99,"rationale":"The sentence defines the 106-patient intention-to-treat analysis population and its group counts."},{"item":"15","pnum":43,"sid":"S99","score":0.96,"rationale":"The sentence reports comparable baseline measurements across groups and identifies the baseline table."},{"item":"17a","pnum":46,"sid":"S106","score":0.83,"rationale":"The figure caption identifies a Kaplan-Meier analysis of the primary renal-function endpoint."},{"item":"17a","pnum":48,"sid":"S109","score":0.94,"rationale":"The sentence reports the relative occurrence rates of the primary renal-function decline across treatment groups."},{"item":"17a","pnum":48,"sid":"S110","score":0.99,"rationale":"The sentence reports primary endpoint event results by group with hazard ratios, confidence intervals, and P values."},{"item":"17b","pnum":48,"sid":"S110","score":0.99,"rationale":"The sentence reports binary primary-endpoint proportions and comparative hazard ratios across randomized groups."},{"item":"17a","pnum":48,"sid":"S111","score":0.96,"rationale":"The sentence reports a significant three-group comparison 