s that proteinuria reduction over time was greatest in the prednisolone plus chlorambucil group."},{"item":"17a","pnum":53,"sid":"S121","score":0.98,"rationale":"The sentence reports the between-group mean difference in urinary-protein reduction and its P value."},{"item":"17a","pnum":53,"sid":"S122","score":0.98,"rationale":"The sentence reports the between-group mean difference in urinary-protein reduction for ciclosporin."},{"item":"19","pnum":54,"sid":"S123","score":0.93,"rationale":"The table caption explicitly identifies serious adverse events by treatment and affected body system."},{"item":"19","pnum":55,"sid":"S124","score":0.99,"rationale":"The sentence reports the total number of adverse events and serious adverse events observed."},{"item":"19","pnum":55,"sid":"S125","score":0.97,"rationale":"The sentence reports that serious adverse events occurred in 54 patients."},{"item":"17a","pnum":55,"sid":"S126","score":0.95,"rationale":"The sentence reports group-specific serious adverse-event results at one year with significance testing."},{"item":"17b","pnum":55,"sid":"S126","score":0.97,"rationale":"The sentence reports binary serious-adverse-event proportions by treatment group."},{"item":"19","pnum":55,"sid":"S126","score":0.99,"rationale":"The sentence reports comparative serious adverse-event findings across treatment groups."},{"item":"19","pnum":56,"sid":"S127","score":0.95,"rationale":"The sentence reports observed haematological adverse events and absence of lymphomas or leukaemias."},{"item":"19","pnum":56,"sid":"S128","score":0.94,"rationale":"The sentence reports dermatological adverse effects including rash and shingles."},{"item":"19","pnum":56,"sid":"S129","score":0.94,"rationale":"The sentence reports renal adverse effects including renal-function deterioration and hyperkalaemia."},{"item":"19","pnum":56,"sid":"S130","score":0.94,"rationale":"The sentence reports neurological adverse effects of tremor and headache."},{"item":"19","pnum":56,"sid":"S131","score":0.95,"rationale":"The sentence reports cardiovascular adverse effects including myocardial infarction and pulmonary embolus."},{"item":"19","pnum":56,"sid":"S132","score":0.94,"rationale":"The sentence reports metabolic adverse effects including impaired glucose tolerance."},{"item":"19","pnum":56,"sid":"S133","score":0.95,"rationale":"The sentence reports gastroenterological adverse effects including nausea, bleeding, and pancreatitis."},{"item":"19","pnum":56,"sid":"S134","score":0.94,"rationale":"The sentence reports infectious adverse events including septicaemia, pneumonia, and cellulitis."},{"item":"19","pnum":56,"sid":"S135","score":0.93,"rationale":"The sentence reports other adverse effects including fracture, hernia repairs, and pulmonary sarcoid."}]}", "recovery_added_pnums": []}, "discussion": {"selected_paragraphs_json": "[{"pnum": 57, "paragraph_text": "Discussion", "sentences": [{"sid": "S137", "text": "Discussion"}]}, {"pnum": 58, "paragraph_text": "These results suggest that supportive therapy plus prednisolone and chlorambucil is better at prevention of decline in excretory renal function than is supportive therapy plus ciclosporin or supportive therapy alone in patients with deteriorating function due to idiopathic membranous nephropathy. Ideally the results should be confirmed in a larger study, but because this trial took 10 years to recruit due to the difficulty of running a multicentre trial in slowly progressive glomerular disease, a similar larger study is unlikely to be done. 92% of all patients in this trial received angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitors, showing that this aspect of supportive therapy was virtually universal in all three groups. The benefit to renal function was matched by a reduction in proteinuria with prednisolone and chlorambucil. In this severely affected subset of patients, we thought it would be unlikely that even responders would achieve complete remission of proteinuria, hence our decision to make excretory renal function our primary endpoint.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S138", "text": "These results suggest that supportive therapy plus prednisolone and chlorambucil is better at prevention of decline in excretory renal function than is supportive therapy plus ciclosporin or supportive therapy alone in patients with deteriorating function due to idiopathic membranous nephropathy."}, {"sid": "S139", "text": "Ideally the results should be confirmed in a larger study, but because this trial took 10 years to recruit due to the difficulty of running a multicentre trial in slowly progressive glomerular disease, a similar larger study is unlikely to be done."}, {"sid": "S140", "text": "92% of all patients in this trial received angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitors, showing that this aspect of supportive therapy was virtually universal in all three groups."}, {"sid": "S141", "text": "The benefit to renal function was matched by a reduction in proteinuria with prednisolone and chlorambucil."}, {"sid": "S142", "text": "In this severely affected subset of patients, we thought it would be unlikely that even responders would achieve complete remission of proteinuria, hence our decision to make excretory renal function our primary endpoint."}]}, {"pnum": 59, "paragraph_text": "Adverse events were frequent, including in the supportive therapy group, suggesting that this group of patients is susceptible to major medical problems. Masking was impossible because of the nature of the treatments involved, but we accept that the fact that the study was unblinded might have affected the reporting of adverse effects. In the active intervention groups, the serious adverse effects were predictable from the side-effect profiles of the drugs—particularly headache, tremor, hypertension, deterioration in renal function, or infection in the ciclosporin group and predominantly haematological (especially leucopenia and anaemia) or metabolic (especially glucose intolerance) effects in the prednisolone and chlorambucil group. Dose adjustment of chlorambucil arose frequently and treatment interruptions were common, both accounting for most of the protocol departures in the prednisolone and chlorambucil group. Similarly, in the ciclosporin group, nephrotoxicity was a substantial problem despite the fact that we used target blood concentrations advocated in a previous RCT;12 dose reductions, treatment interruptions, and reaching of primary endpoint were frequent in this group.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S143", "text": "Adverse events were frequent, including in the supportive therapy group, suggesting that this group of patients is susceptible to major medical problems."}, {"sid": "S144", "text": "Masking was impossible because of the nature of the treatments involved, but we accept that the fact that the study was unblinded might have affected the reporting of adverse effects."}, {"sid": "S145", "text": "In the active intervention groups, the serious adverse effects were predictable from the side-effect profiles of the drugs—particularly headache, tremor, hypertension, deterioration in renal function, or infection in the ciclosporin group and predominantly haematological (especially leucopenia and anaemia) or metabolic (especially glucose intolerance) effects in the prednisolone and chlorambucil group."}, {"sid": "S146", "text": "Dose adjustment of chlorambucil arose frequently and treatment interruptions were common, both accounting for most of the protocol departures in the prednisolone and chlorambucil group."}, {"sid": "S147", "text": "Similarly, in the ciclosporin group, nephrotoxicity was a substantial problem despite the fact that we used target blood concentrations advocated in a previous RCT;12 dose reductions, treatment interruptions, and reaching of primary endpoint were frequent in this group."}]}, {"pnum": 60, "paragraph_text": "Slow trial recruitment was undoubtedly determined by the eligibility criteria: deteriorating renal function in idiopathic membranous nephropathy has become less common with angiotensin-cascade blockade and other aspects of supportive management,16 and our detailed communications with renal units throughout the UK during the trial showed that the rarity of eligible patients was the main barrier to recruitment. Of the 37 units that entered patients, 31 recruited four patients or fewer. Renal units that declined to participate and apply for ethical approval were roughly equally divided into those concerned about the lack of active therapy in the supportive care only group or the potential toxicity of active therapy—clear evidence that considerable uncertainty surrounds appropriate management of this disorder, and that a definitive RCT is needed.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S148", "text": "Slow trial recruitment was undoubtedly determined by the eligibility criteria: deteriorating renal function in idiopathic membranous nephropathy has become less common with angiotensin-cascade blockade and other aspects of supportive management,16 and our detailed communications with renal units throughout the UK during the trial showed that the rarity of eligible patients was the main barrier to recruitment."}, {"sid": "S149", "text": "Of the 37 units that entered patients, 31 recruited four patients or fewer."}, {"sid": "S150", "text": "Renal units that declined to participate and apply for ethical approval were roughly equally divided into those concerned about the lack of active therapy in the supportive care only group or the potential toxicity of active therapy—clear evidence that considerable uncertainty surrounds appropriate management of this disorder, and that a definitive RCT is needed."}]}, {"pnum": 61, "paragraph_text": "We contend that for patients with idiopathic membranous nephropathy, 6 months' therapy with alternating monthly cycles of prednisolone and chlorambucil is the treatment approach best supported by evidence, and our study extends this evidence to the important subset of patients with membranous nephropathy and deteriorating excretory renal function. Our findings do not support the use of ciclosporin in this group—the adverse effects on renal function make it unsuitable once renal function has started to decline. The ciclosporin starting dose in our study was based on an RCT reported by Cattran and colleagues.12 A later trial led by this group17 used a lower starting dose (3·5 mg/kg per day) but aimed for similar plasma concentrations and reported beneficial effects on proteinuria. Other investigators have used a lower dose of ciclosporin in small uncontrolled studies and also reported beneficial effects for proteinuria.18,19", "sentences": [{"sid": "S151", "text": "We contend that for patients with idiopathic membranous nephropathy, 6 months' therapy with alternating monthly cycles of prednisolone and chlorambucil is the treatment approach best supported by evidence, and our study extends this evidence to the important subset of patients with membranous nephropathy and deteriorating excretory renal function."}, {"sid": "S152", "text": "Our findings do not support the use of ciclosporin in this group—the adverse effects on renal function make it unsuitable once renal function has started to decline."}, {"sid": "S153", "text": "The ciclosporin starting dose in our study was based on an RCT reported by Cattran and colleagues.12"}, {"sid": "S154", "text": "A later trial led by this group17 used a lower starting dose (3·5 mg/kg per day) but aimed for similar plasma concentrations and reported beneficial effects on proteinuria."}, {"sid": "S155", "text": "Other investigators have used a lower dose of ciclosporin in small uncontrolled studies and also reported beneficial effects for proteinuria.18,19"}]}, {"pnum": 62, "paragraph_text": "Shortly after our study started, Ponticelli and colleagues20 reported that the choice of alkylating agent (between chlorambucil and the more familiar cyclophosphamide) for idiopathic membranous nephropathy might be immaterial, although cyclophosphamide might be less toxic. We decided not to change our study design, but we agree that cyclophosphamide could probably be substituted for chlorambucil. Uncontrolled studies using a combination of prednisolone and cyclophosphamide in severely affected patients have led to similar conclusions,1,21 and one RCT supports this approach in patients with well preserved renal function at entry.22 Our study shows that this form of therapy can still be effective in patients whose renal function has started to deteriorate. The use of alkylating agents (with their potent effects on B lymphocytes) for idiopathic membranous nephropathy has a rationale now that autoantibodies to PLA2R1 have been discovered in most patients.8,9 Immunosuppressive therapy is also logical in view of our previously published analysis of the genetic basis of idiopathic membranous nephropathy,10 showing that two genes predispose white people to this disorder, an immune-response ...", "sentences": [{"sid": "S156", "text": "Shortly after our study started, Ponticelli and colleagues20 reported that the choice of alkylating agent (between chlorambucil and the more familiar cyclophosphamide) for idiopathic membranous nephropathy might be immaterial, although cyclophosphamide might be less toxic."}, {"sid": "S157", "text": "We decided not to change our study design, but we agree that cyclophosphamide could probably be substituted for chlorambucil."}, {"sid": "S158", "text": "Uncontrolled studies using a combination of prednisolone and cyclophosphamide in severely affected patients have led to similar conclusions,1,21 and one RCT supports this approach in patients with well preserved renal function at entry.22"}, {"sid": "S159", "text": "Our study shows that this form of therapy can still be effective in patients whose renal function has started to deteriorate."}, {"sid": "S160", "text": "The use of alkylating agents (with their potent effects on B lymphocytes) for idiopathic membranous nephropathy has a rationale now that autoantibodies to PLA2R1 have been discovered in most patients.8,9"}, {"sid": "S161", "text": "Immunosuppressive therapy is also logical in view of our previously published analysis of the genetic basis of idiopathic membranous nephropathy,10 showing that two genes predispose white people to this disorder, an immune-response gene in the HLA-DQA1 region and the PLA2R1 gene itself."}]}, {"pnum": 63, "paragraph_text": "Rituximab for idiopathic membranous nephropathy has shown promise,23,24 but so far evidence for its effectiveness is not based on RCT data and the beneficial effects are mostly in reduction of proteinuria rather than preservation of excretory renal function. Furthermore, rituximab is expensive and is associated with important long-term safety concerns such as progressive multifocal leukoencephalopathy.25 However, progressive multifocal leukoencephalopathy has not been reported in patients with idiopathic membranous nephropathy given rituximab and might be associated with intensity of immunosuppression, since patients who got the disease received rituximab together with other agents. Future RCTs should assess the cost-effectiveness, efficacy, and safety of rituximab for patients with idiopathic membranous nephropathy, perhaps compared with prednisolone plus an alkylating agent (either cyclophosphamide or chlorambucil). Future trials should ideally include patient-reported outcomes and an analysis of the balance between treatment costs (including those associated with adverse effects) and costs of renal replacement therapy in untreated patients, so that the cost–benefit of delaying t ...", "sentences": [{"sid": "S162", "text": "Rituximab for idiopathic membranous nephropathy has shown promise,23,24 but so far evidence for its effectiveness is not based on RCT data and the beneficial effects are mostly in reduction of proteinuria rather than preservation of excretory renal function."}, {"sid": "S163", "text": "Furthermore, rituximab is expensive and is associated with important long-term safety concerns such as progressive multifocal leukoencephalopathy.25"}, {"sid": "S164", "text": "However, progressive multifocal leukoencephalopathy has not been reported in patients with idiopathic membranous nephropathy given rituximab and might be associated with intensity of immunosuppression, since patients who got the disease received rituximab together with other agents."}, {"sid": "S165", "text": "Future RCTs should assess the cost-effectiveness, efficacy, and safety of rituximab for patients with idiopathic membranous nephropathy, perhaps compared with prednisolone plus an alkylating agent (either cyclophosphamide or chlorambucil)."}, {"sid": "S166", "text": "Future trials should ideally include patient-reported outcomes and an analysis of the balance between treatment costs (including those associated with adverse effects) and costs of renal replacement therapy in untreated patients, so that the cost–benefit of delaying the need for renal replacement therapy and quality-of-life issues can be assessed."}]}, {"pnum": 64, "paragraph_text": "Adverse effects, particularly haematological outcomes, were common in patients given prednisolone and chlorambucil in our study and often necessitated dose reduction or interruption of therapy. Clearly, the preservation of renal function that can be achieved with prednisolone and chlorambucil comes at a price, and careful monitoring of the therapy is needed.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S167", "text": "Adverse effects, particularly haematological outcomes, were common in patients given prednisolone and chlorambucil in our study and often necessitated dose reduction or interruption of therapy."}, {"sid": "S168", "text": "Clearly, the preservation of renal function that can be achieved with prednisolone and chlorambucil comes at a price, and careful monitoring of the therapy is needed."}]}, {"pnum": 65, "paragraph_text": "Panel", "sentences": [{"sid": "S169", "text": "Panel"}]}, {"pnum": 66, "paragraph_text": "Research in context", "sentences": [{"sid": "S170", "text": "Research in context"}]}, {"pnum": 67, "paragraph_text": "Systematic review", "sentences": [{"sid": "S171", "text": "Systematic review"}]}, {"pnum": 68, "paragraph_text": "We searched Medline and PubMed for articles published in any language between Jan 1, 1960, and April 12, 2012, with the keywords “membranous nephropathy” or “membranous glomerulonephritis” and “treatment”, “trial”, and “randomised”. The older scientific literature is best summarised in a 2004 Cochrane review26 and the current literature is well reviewed in a 2012 authoritative guideline on the treatment of glomerulonephritis.27", "sentences": [{"sid": "S172", "text": "We searched Medline and PubMed for articles published in any language between Jan 1, 1960, and April 12, 2012, with the keywords “membranous nephropathy” or “membranous glomerulonephritis” and “treatment”, “trial”, and “randomised”."}, {"sid": "S173", "text": "The older scientific literature is best summarised in a 2004 Cochrane review26 and the current literature is well reviewed in a 2012 authoritative guideline on the treatment of glomerulonephritis.27"}]}, {"pnum": 69, "paragraph_text": "Interpretation", "sentences": [{"sid": "S174", "text": "Interpretation"}]}, {"pnum": 70, "paragraph_text": "This study is the first to focus on the important subset of patients with membranous nephropathy whose excretory renal function is deteriorating. The results suggest that therapy with prednisolone and chlorambucil is better than with ciclosporin or supportive therapy alone. This patient population has serious morbidity, and the benefits of treatment need to be weighed against the adverse events. The protection of renal function offered by prednisolone and chlorambucil comes at a price, so this therapy needs to be closely monitored.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S175", "text": "This study is the first to focus on the important subset of patients with membranous nephropathy whose excretory renal function is deteriorating."}, {"sid": "S176", "text": "The results suggest that therapy with prednisolone and chlorambucil is better than with ciclosporin or supportive therapy alone."}, {"sid": "S177", "text": "This patient population has serious morbidity, and the benefits of treatment need to be weighed against the adverse events."}, {"sid": "S178", "text": "The protection of renal function offered by prednisolone and chlorambucil comes at a price, so this therapy needs to be closely monitored."}]}, {"pnum": 71, "paragraph_text": "Benefits of prednisolone and chlorambucil were maintained for at least 3 years of follow-up. Delaying end-stage renal disease, with its associated cardiovascular risk and increased morbidity and mortality, is of undoubted value to patients with idiopathic membranous nephropathy. However, even in patients given prednisolone and chlorambucil, only 40% had not had a further 20% decline in excretory renal function at 3 years. Clearly, more effective and safer forms of therapy are still needed for idiopathic membranous nephropathy. Until new treatments are available and have been properly tested, the evidence favours use of prednisolone and an alkylating agent in the most severely affected patients. This conclusion, and the lack of good RCTs in nephrology to address this and similar questions, are supported by a Cochrane review of the subject26 and an authoritative review of the international scientific literature on the treatment of glomerulonephritis (panel).27", "sentences": [{"sid": "S179", "text": "Benefits of prednisolone and chlorambucil were maintained for at least 3 years of follow-up."}, {"sid": "S180", "text": "Delaying end-stage renal disease, with its associated cardiovascular risk and increased morbidity and mortality, is of undoubted value to patients with idiopathic membranous nephropathy."}, {"sid": "S181", "text": "However, even in patients given prednisolone and chlorambucil, only 40% had not had a further 20% decline in excretory renal function at 3 years."}, {"sid": "S182", "text": "Clearly, more effective and safer forms of therapy are still needed for idiopathic membranous nephropathy."}, {"sid": "S183", "text": "Until new treatments are available and have been properly tested, the evidence favours use of prednisolone and an alkylating agent in the most severely affected patients."}, {"sid": "S184", "text": "This conclusion, and the lack of good RCTs in nephrology to address this and similar questions, are supported by a Cochrane review of the subject26 and an authoritative review of the international scientific literature on the treatment of glomerulonephritis (panel).27"}]}, {"pnum": 72, "paragraph_text": "The supportive therapy only group effectively continued current treatment whereas the two intervention groups received new treatment, which led to some minor differences in the time between randomisation and baseline readings (ie, initiation of treatment); however, the time differences were small in the context of this slowly progressive disease in comparison with the length of follow-up, and as a result the risk of bias is small.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S185", "text": "The supportive therapy only group effectively continued current treatment whereas the two intervention groups received new treatment, which led to some minor differences in the time between randomisation and baseline readings (ie, initiation of treatment); however, the time differences were small in the context of this slowly progressive disease in comparison with the length of follow-up, and as a result the risk of bias is small."}]}, {"pnum": 73, "paragraph_text": "Recruitment was very slow and the trial was designed over 14 years ago. However, we believe that the trial results are still relevant, not least because few RCTs of drugs for this disease have been done, with none in the subset of patients with deteriorating excretory renal function.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S186", "text": "Recruitment was very slow and the trial was designed over 14 years ago."}, {"sid": "S187", "text": "However, we believe that the trial results are still relevant, not least because few RCTs of drugs for this disease have been done, with none in the subset of patients with deteriorating excretory renal function."}]}, {"pnum": 74, "paragraph_text": "One aspect of the slow recruitment was the changes in methods that became established during the trial, both for estimation of excretory kidney function and assessment of proteinuria. We used one consistent method for the calculation of primary endpoints. We did not use gold-standard methods of measuring kidney function such as isotope clearance studies. These methods are expensive and invasive, and although our trial depended on estimations, we believe it is relevant to everyday clinical practice since we used standard estimation techniques that are used in nephrology practice worldwide.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S188", "text": "One aspect of the slow recruitment was the changes in methods that became established during the trial, both for estimation of excretory kidney function and assessment of proteinuria."}, {"sid": "S189", "text": "We used one consistent method for the calculation of primary endpoints."}, {"sid": "S190", "text": "We did not use gold-standard methods of measuring kidney function such as isotope clearance studies."}, {"sid": "S191", "text": "These methods are expensive and invasive, and although our trial depended on estimations, we believe it is relevant to everyday clinical practice since we used standard estimation techniques that are used in nephrology practice worldwide."}]}, {"pnum": 75, "paragraph_text": "In this study we assessed ciclosporin monotherapy and noted that the drug's nephrotoxicity, even at blood concentrations advocated in a previous RCT,12,15 was harmful in the severely affected subset that we selected. Some physicians advocate use of ciclosporin together with prednisolone, but we know of no good evidence that this combination reduces renal toxicity.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S192", "text": "In this study we assessed ciclosporin monotherapy and noted that the drug's nephrotoxicity, even at blood concentrations advocated in a previous RCT,12,15 was harmful in the severely affected subset that we selected."}, {"sid": "S193", "text": "Some physicians advocate use of ciclosporin together with prednisolone, but we know of no good evidence that this combination reduces renal toxicity."}]}, {"pnum": 76, "paragraph_text": "We need to follow up these patients for even longer to absolutely assess the value of the delay to end-stage renal disease that we noted in the prednisolone and chlorambucil group and to gather longer-term data for delayed adverse effects in the two intervention groups, especially lymphomas and other malignancies.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S194", "text": "We need to follow up these patients for even longer to absolutely assess the value of the delay to end-stage renal disease that we noted in the prednisolone and chlorambucil group and to gather longer-term data for delayed adverse effects in the two intervention groups, especially lymphomas and other malignancies."}]}]", "extraction_output_json": "{"article_id":"PMC3590447","section":"discussion","extractions":[{"item":"22","pnum":58,"sid":"S138","score":0.98,"rationale":"The sentence interprets the trial results as showing superior preservation of renal function with prednisolone and chlorambucil."},{"item":"22","pnum":58,"sid":"S141","score":0.9,"rationale":"The sentence interprets the renal-function benefit by relating it to reduced proteinuria with prednisolone and chlorambucil."},{"item":"22","pnum":59,"sid":"S143","score":0.86,"rationale":"The sentence interprets frequent adverse events as evidence that this patient group is susceptible to major medical problems."},{"item":"20","pnum":59,"sid":"S144","score":0.99,"rationale":"The unblinded study design is identified as a potential source of biased adverse-effect reporting."},{"item":"22","pnum":59,"sid":"S147","score":0.9,"rationale":"The sentence interprets ciclosporin safety findings as showing substantial nephrotoxicity despite recommended target concentrations."},{"item":"22","pnum":60,"sid":"S150","score":0.88,"rationale":"The sentence interprets participating centres' concerns as evidence of management uncertainty and need for a definitive trial."},{"item":"22","pnum":61,"sid":"S151","score":0.96,"rationale":"The sentence interprets the evidence as supporting prednisolone and chlorambucil for patients with deteriorating renal function."},{"item":"22","pnum":61,"sid":"S152","score":0.98,"rationale":"The sentence interprets the findings as not supporting ciclosporin because its renal adverse effects make it unsuitable."},{"item":"22","pnum":62,"sid":"S159","score":0.94,"rationale":"The sentence interprets the study as showing therapy remains effective after renal function has begun deteriorating."},{"item":"22","pnum":64,"sid":"S168","score":0.99,"rationale":"The sentence explicitly balances renal-function preservation against treatment harms and recommends careful monitoring."},{"item":"20","pnum":72,"sid":"S185","score":0.94,"rationale":"The sentence addresses minor baseline-timing differences between groups and evaluates their potential risk of bias."},{"item":"22","pnum":73,"sid":"S187","score":0.91,"rationale":"The sentence interprets the trial as still relevant in light of the scarcity of comparable drug trials."},{"item":"20","pnum":74,"sid":"S190","score":0.96,"rationale":"The sentence identifies use of non-gold-standard kidney-function measurement as a specific study limitation."},{"item":"21","pnum":74,"sid":"S191","score":0.96,"rationale":"The sentence explicitly states that the trial's standard estimation methods make it relevant to clinical practice worldwide."},{"item":"22","pnum":75,"sid":"S192","score":0.94,"rationale":"The sentence interprets the trial's ciclosporin findings as harmful nephrotoxicity in the selected severely affected patients."},{"item":"20","pnum":76,"sid":"S194","score":0.96,"rationale":"The sentence identifies insufficient follow-up to fully assess delayed renal and adverse-effect outcomes."}]}", "recovery_added_pnums": []}, "other_information": {"selected_paragraphs_json": "[{"pnum": 6, "paragraph_text": "This randomised controlled trial was undertaken in 37 renal units across the UK. We recruited patients (18–75 years) with biopsy-proven idiopathic membranous nephropathy, a plasma creatinine concentration of less than 300 μmol/L, and at least a 20% decline in excretory renal function measured in the 2 years before study entry, based on at least three measurements over a period of 3 months or longer. Patients were randomly assigned (1:1:1) by a random number table to receive supportive treatment only, supportive treatment plus 6 months of alternating cycles of prednisolone and chlorambucil, or supportive treatment plus 12 months of ciclosporin. The primary outcome was a further 20% decline in renal function from baseline, analysed by intention to treat. The trial is registered as an International Standard Randomised Controlled Trial, number 99959692.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S9", "text": "This randomised controlled trial was undertaken in 37 renal units across the UK."}, {"sid": "S10", "text": "We recruited patients (18–75 years) with biopsy-proven idiopathic membranous nephropathy, a plasma creatinine concentration of less than 300 μmol/L, and at least a 20% decline in excretory renal function measured in the 2 years before study entry, based on at least three measurements over a period of 3 months or longer."}, {"sid": "S11", "text": "Patients were randomly assigned (1:1:1) by a random number table to receive supportive treatment only, supportive treatment plus 6 months of alternating cycles of prednisolone and chlorambucil, or supportive treatment plus 12 months of ciclosporin."}, {"sid": "S12", "text": "The primary outcome was a further 20% decline in renal function from baseline, analysed by intention to treat."}, {"sid": "S13", "text": "The trial is registered as an International Standard Randomised Controlled Trial, number 99959692."}]}, {"pnum": 12, "paragraph_text": "Medical Research Council, Novartis, Renal Association, Kidney Research UK.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S24", "text": "Medical Research Council, Novartis, Renal Association, Kidney Research UK."}]}, {"pnum": 22, "paragraph_text": "Ethics approval was obtained from the South West Multicentre Research Ethics Committee (reference MREC/97/6/12). Each participating centre also obtained local ethical approval. All patients gave written informed consent.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S45", "text": "Ethics approval was obtained from the South West Multicentre Research Ethics Committee (reference MREC/97/6/12)."}, {"sid": "S46", "text": "Each participating centre also obtained local ethical approval."}, {"sid": "S47", "text": "All patients gave written informed consent."}]}, {"pnum": 36, "paragraph_text": "In 2003, the trial was shown to comply with the requirements of the EU clinical trials directive, and in 2004, a clinical trial authorisation (CTA) was obtained from the Medicines and Healthcare products Regulatory Authority (CTA number 18524/0001/001). In 2008, the trial was adopted onto the National Institute for Health Research portfolio and assigned the UK Clinical Research Network identification number 2579. The trial is registered as an International Standard Randomised Controlled Trial, number 99959692.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S86", "text": "In 2003, the trial was shown to comply with the requirements of the EU clinical trials directive, and in 2004, a clinical trial authorisation (CTA) was obtained from the Medicines and Healthcare products Regulatory Authority (CTA number 18524/0001/001)."}, {"sid": "S87", "text": "In 2008, the trial was adopted onto the National Institute for Health Research portfolio and assigned the UK Clinical Research Network identification number 2579."}, {"sid": "S88", "text": "The trial is registered as an International Standard Randomised Controlled Trial, number 99959692."}]}, {"pnum": 37, "paragraph_text": "Role of the funding source", "sentences": [{"sid": "S89", "text": "Role of the funding source"}]}, {"pnum": 38, "paragraph_text": "The sponsors of the study had no role in study design, data collection, data analysis, data interpretation, or writing of the report. The corresponding author had full access to all the data in the study and had final responsibility to submit for publication.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S90", "text": "The sponsors of the study had no role in study design, data collection, data analysis, data interpretation, or writing of the report."}, {"sid": "S91", "text": "The corresponding author had full access to all the data in the study and had final responsibility to submit for publication."}]}, {"pnum": 77, "paragraph_text": "Back matter", "sentences": [{"sid": "S195", "text": "Back matter"}]}, {"pnum": 78, "paragraph_text": "Acknowledgments", "sentences": [{"sid": "S196", "text": "Acknowledgments"}]}, {"pnum": 79, "paragraph_text": "The trial was largely funded by two grants from the Medical Research Council (MRC; grant reference G9721265). Before MRC funding was obtained, a small unrestricted grant from Novartis supported the purchase of trial record books and some other trial materials. Additional contributions to continuation funding came from Kidney Research UK and the Renal Association. The drug treatments, investigations, and clinic visits were not funded by the trial, they were all provided as part of routine clinical management.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S197", "text": "The trial was largely funded by two grants from the Medical Research Council (MRC; grant reference G9721265)."}, {"sid": "S198", "text": "Before MRC funding was obtained, a small unrestricted grant from Novartis supported the purchase of trial record books and some other trial materials."}, {"sid": "S199", "text": "Additional contributions to continuation funding came from Kidney Research UK and the Renal Association."}, {"sid": "S200", "text": "The drug treatments, investigations, and clinic visits were not funded by the trial, they were all provided as part of routine clinical management."}]}, {"pnum": 80, "paragraph_text": "Contributors", "sentences": [{"sid": "S201", "text": "Contributors"}]}, {"pnum": 81, "paragraph_text": "The trial was conceived and designed by members of the UK Renal Association Clinical Trials Committee's glomerulonephritis subgroup, chaired by PWM (the principal investigator), who was the sole applicant on funding applications to the UK Medical Research Council. All authors helped to write the report and commented on the manuscript. AH analysed the data and advised on statistical issues at the time of the trial write up. TLC was the trial administrator; obtained the data; and prepared communications with participating centres, the data monitoring committee, and funders. MML and CF were research nurses responsible for recruitment and return of data. DA, JF, GJG, DRWJ, DO'D, MB-J, and PWM designed the trial. PWM took overall responsibility for communications during the trial, analysed the data, and wrote the first draft of the report.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S202", "text": "The trial was conceived and designed by members of the UK Renal Association Clinical Trials Committee's glomerulonephritis subgroup, chaired by PWM (the principal investigator), who was the sole applicant on funding applications to the UK Medical Research Council."}, {"sid": "S203", "text": "All authors helped to write the report and commented on the manuscript."}, {"sid": "S204", "text": "AH analysed the data and advised on statistical issues at the time of the trial write up."}, {"sid": "S205", "text": "TLC was the trial administrator; obtained the data; and prepared communications with participating centres, the data monitoring committee, and funders."}, {"sid": "S206", "text": "MML and CF were research nurses responsible for recruitment and return of data."}, {"sid": "S207", "text": "DA, JF, GJG, DRWJ, DO'D, MB-J, and PWM designed the trial."}, {"sid": "S208", "text": "PWM took overall responsibility for communications during the trial, analysed the data, and wrote the first draft of the report."}]}, {"pnum": 82, "paragraph_text": "Conflicts of interest", "sentences": [{"sid": "S209", "text": "Conflicts of interest"}]}, {"pnum": 83, "paragraph_text": "We declare that we have no conflicts of interest.", "sentences": [{"sid": "S210", "text": "We declare that we have no conflicts of interest."}]}]", "extraction_output_json": "{"article_id":"PMC3590447","section":"other_information","extractions":[{"item":"23","pnum":36,"sid":"S88","score":0.99,"rationale":"The sentence gives the International Standard Randomised Controlled Trial registration and number 99959692."},{"item":"25","pnum":38,"sid":"S90","score":0.98,"rationale":"The sentence explicitly states that the study sponsors had no role in design, data, interpretation, or reporting."},{"item":"25","pnum":79,"sid":"S197","score":0.99,"rationale":"The sentence identifies Medical Research Council grants as the trial's primary funding source."},{"item":"25","pnum":79,"sid":"S198","score":0.99,"rationale":"The sentence reports an unrestricted Novartis grant supporting trial record books and other trial materials."},{"item":"25","pnum":79,"sid":"S199","score":0.99,"rationale":"The sentence identifies Kidney Research UK and the Renal Association as contributors to continuation funding."}]}", "recovery_added_pnums": []}}
